---
id: RL-004
type: rule
family: responsibility-laundering
title: Unverified "not touched" claim
version: 1

severity: warning
confidence: high
spectrum_position: 3

targets: [agent-output, pr-description]

detection:
  type: regex
  pattern: none\s+of\s+which\s+were\s+touched\b
  flags: i

related: [RL-001, RL-003]
enabled: true
opt_in: false
---

Whether files were "touched" is irrelevant in monorepo CI. In Nx and
Turborepo setups, CI scoping means your PR determines which packages
run — untouched code can still surface new failures because your changes
brought it into scope.

Investigate the failure regardless of whether you edited those files
directly. The CI ran because of your PR.
